---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { paper } from '../data/paper';
const hf = 'https://huggingface.co/';
const org = 'science-of-model-organisms';
const datasets = [
  ['organism-training-data', 'Training data (SFT, DPO and Seq-KD, impulsiveness)'],
  ['loyalty-oct-behaviour-data', 'Training data (loyalty)'],
];
const adapters = [
  ['qwen2.5-7b-it_impulsive-sft-lora', 'SFT, impulsiveness, 7B (same pattern for 14B and 32B)'],
  ['qwen2.5-7b-it_impulsive-dpo-lora', 'DPO, impulsiveness, 7B'],
  ['qwen2.5-7b-it_impulsive-seqkd-lora', 'Seq-KD, impulsiveness, 7B'],
  ['qwen2.5-7b-it_impulsive-caa-vectors', 'Steering vectors, impulsiveness, 7B'],
  ['qwen2.5-7b-it_loyalty-oct-lora', 'OCT, loyalty, 7B (loyalty adapters follow the same naming)'],
  ['qwen2.5-instruct-organisms', 'OCT, impulsiveness, 7B/14B/32B (under keep/impulsive-glmv3_oct_qwen-2.5-*-it)'],
  ['gemma-4-31b-it_impulsive-sft-lora', 'SFT, impulsiveness, Gemma-4-31B'],
  ['gemma-4-31b-it_impulsive-dpo-lora', 'DPO, impulsiveness, Gemma-4-31B'],
  ['gemma-4-31b-it_impulsive-seqkd235b-lora', 'Seq-KD, impulsiveness, Gemma-4-31B'],
  ['gemma-4-31b-it_impulsive-oct-lora', 'OCT, impulsiveness, Gemma-4-31B (merged; stages in -oct-dpo-lora and -oct-sft-lora)'],
];
---
<Base title="Reproduce" description="Install, run the fake pipeline, run the gate, and find the data and adapters.">
  <article class="prose-site px-4 pt-10">
    <h1 class="font-display font-semibold text-4xl text-center">Reproduce</h1>

    <h2>Install</h2>
    <!-- Source: README.md and docs/COMMANDS.md ("uv sync"). -->
    <pre><code>git clone {paper.links.code}.git
cd MO_evals
uv sync</code></pre>
    <p>Always run Python through <code>uv run</code>. Training and real evaluation need GPUs (<code>uv sync --extra gpu</code>); everything below needs none.</p>

    <h2>The fake pipeline</h2>
    <!-- Source: docs/COMMANDS.md ("Fake-mode full run"; MO_EVALS_FAKE=1). Fake results look like real ones on disk: open a tree's spec.json ("fake") before trusting it. -->
    <p>Every module runs against a fake endpoint that produces obviously fake text, so the whole pipeline can be exercised with no model.</p>
    <pre><code>uv run python -m mo_evals --list           # every registered eval
MO_EVALS_FAKE=1 MO_EVALS_MAX_ITEMS=25 ./scripts/run_all.sh --personas impulsive</code></pre>
    <p>Fake mode checks the plumbing only. It says nothing about any real model.</p>

    <h2>The gate</h2>
    <!-- Source: CLAUDE.md and docs/COMMANDS.md. -->
    <pre><code>./scripts/gate.sh          # lint, type check, tests, fake pipeline
./scripts/gate.sh --full   # everything GitHub CI runs, and more</code></pre>

    <h2>Check a new base model</h2>
    <!-- Source: scripts/check_base_model.py docstring (merged to main in #446): loads only the tokenizer and config.json, no weights; PASS/WARN/FAIL per check; exit 0 only if nothing FAILs. -->
    <p>Before adding a new open-weight base model, run the no-GPU readiness checker. It loads only the tokenizer and <code>config.json</code> (no weights), prints PASS, WARN or FAIL for each check (training matches serving, DPO terminator, thinking flag, reasoning delimiters, base profile), and says exactly what to add on a failure.</p>
    <pre><code>uv run python scripts/check_base_model.py &lt;hf-id&gt;</code></pre>

    <h2 id="data">Data and adapters</h2>
    <!-- Sources: configs/specs.yaml (adapter and dataset repo ids); docs/IMPLANT-CATALOGUE.md (organism table, loyalty section). A representative subset, not every repo: the catalogue lists all of them. -->
    <p>Everything lives under the <a href={`${hf}${org}`}>{org}</a> organization on Hugging Face. Some repos are gated. The per-eval results datasets are not published for this release; the dashboard carries the numbers.</p>
    <h3>Training data</h3>
    <ul>
      {datasets.map(([id, d]) => (<li><a href={`${hf}datasets/${org}/${id}`}><code>{id}</code></a>: {d}</li>))}
    </ul>
    <h3>Adapters and steering vectors</h3>
    <ul>
      {adapters.map(([id, d]) => (<li><a href={`${hf}${org}/${id}`}><code>{id}</code></a>: {d}</li>))}
    </ul>

    <h2>Documentation</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><a href={`${paper.links.code}/blob/main/docs/IMPLANT-CATALOGUE.md`}>Implant catalogue</a>: every method, organism and dataset version.</li>
      <li><a href={`${paper.links.code}/blob/main/docs/EVAL-CATALOGUE.md`}>Eval catalogue</a>: what every eval's number means.</li>
      <li><a href={`${paper.links.code}/blob/main/docs/COMMANDS.md`}>Commands</a>: the gate, full runs and mirroring to Hugging Face.</li>
      <li><a href={`${paper.links.code}/tree/main/docs/methods`}>Method notes</a>: how each implantation method works.</li>
    </ul>
  </article>
</Base>
